## 2. Daily Docker commands

These are the commands you'll use most frequently.

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Start existing container | `sudo docker start diffbot_jazzy` |
| Enter Docker terminal | `sudo docker exec -it diffbot_jazzy bash` |
| Open another Docker terminal | `sudo docker exec -it diffbot_jazzy bash` |
| Exit current Docker terminal | `exit` |
| Stop container | `sudo docker stop diffbot_jazzy` |
| Restart container | `sudo docker restart diffbot_jazzy` |
| List running containers | `sudo docker ps` |
| List all containers | `sudo docker ps -a` |
| View container logs | `sudo docker logs diffbot_jazzy` |
| Delete container | `sudo docker rm -f diffbot_jazzy` |
| Check Docker images | `sudo docker images` |

**Remember:** `exit` from an `exec` terminal does not stop the main container.

