# 7. Docker file management

Your laptop folder:

```text
~/diffbot_jazzy_data
```

is available inside Docker as:

```text
/data
```

Anything saved in `/data` remains available after restarting or recreating the container.

### Copy a file into Docker

From your laptop:

```bash
sudo docker cp myfile.txt diffbot_jazzy:/root/
```

### Copy a file from Docker

```bash
sudo docker cp diffbot_jazzy:/root/myfile.txt ~/
```

### Check disk usage

```bash
sudo docker system df
```

### Remove unused stopped containers

```bash
sudo docker container prune
```

Be careful with cleanup commands: they may remove containers you intended to keep.

